This repository contains the BpiRouter management application: a Go backend
(bpirouter-apid) and a Vue web interface. It is proprietary software. No licence
is granted except as stated below or by separate written agreement.


1. RELATIONSHIP TO THE FIRMWARE'S FREE SOFTWARE

This application ships inside firmware built on OpenWrt, which contains software
under the GNU General Public License and other free software licences.

This application is an independent program, not a derivative of them:

  - the backend is built with CGO_ENABLED=0 and links no C library;
  - its only dependencies are golang-jwt/jwt (MIT) and tredoe/osutil (MPL-2.0);
  - it interacts with the system by executing separate programs (uci, ubus and
    other command-line tools), never by linking into them or being loaded into
    their address space.

It is therefore an aggregate alongside the GPL-covered components rather than a
work derived from them, and this licence does not extend to any of them. The
corresponding source for those components is provided as described in
the README supplied with this source.

Nothing in this licence restricts, or is capable of restricting, what a
recipient may do with the GPL-covered parts of the firmware.


2. WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES NOT COVER

  - the OpenWrt sources, feeds and package recipes;
  - the patches to Linux, U-Boot, ARM Trusted Firmware and OpenWrt in
    bpirouter-build/patches/;
  - the build and installation scripts and board configuration in
    bpirouter-build/;
  - the firmware images themselves, to the extent they contain the above.

Each of those carries its own licence. See the LICENSING.md files in
bpirouter-build and bpirouter-feeds.


